From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:45:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Twist GTSAM smoother: slope-aware odometry and predicted z

The smoother accumulated the twist's forward speed as planar motion and
seeded NDT with the last NDT z. Give predict() the last NDT roll and
pitch: only cos(pitch) of the speed is planar odometry, the rest moves
the predicted z of the seed, and the body yaw rate turns the heading
at cos(roll) / cos(pitch). The window stays planar (Pose2); z, roll and
pitch still come from NDT. With roll = pitch = 0 the arithmetic is the
old one: 100 random level-ground runs gave bit-identical seeds, poses
and z against main. Add the smoother's first tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GXUTxp1jp6iH1mo1Uzq365
